# oracle: fix wall/body/polyhedron (zplane wall at z 0, no history) with fix nve/body and fix gravity, pair body/rounded/polyhedron, from examples/body/in.cubes and in.pour3d cut down: 2x2x1 replicate of data.cubes (4 cubes at rest, box 12 x 12 x 6, boundary p p f), gravity 1 along -z, c_n 20, c_t 5, mu 0, A_ua 1, cut 0.5, wall k_n 2000 c_n 50 c_t 50, 3000 steps. Measured with native LAMMPS (black box): engine vs native max relative error 3.5e-12 (ke, step 3000) over the thermo rows.
# oracle-inputs: w121body_cubes_example.data
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-8 abs=1e-12
units           lj
dimension       3
boundary        p p f
atom_style      body rounded/polyhedron 1 10
read_data       w121body_cubes_example.data
replicate       2 2 1
comm_modify     vel yes
pair_style      body/rounded/polyhedron 20 5 0 1 0.5
pair_coeff      * * 100 1
neighbor        0.5 bin
neigh_modify    every 1 delay 0 check yes
timestep        0.001
fix             1 all nve/body
fix             2 all gravity 1.0 vector 0.0 0.0 -1.0
fix             3 all wall/body/polyhedron 2000 50 50 zplane 0.0 NULL
thermo_style    custom step ke pe etotal press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          300
run             3000
